# Next.js 13+ App Router Patterns

## Overview
Best practices for the Next.js App Router (app directory) introduced in Next.js 13+.

## Server vs Client Components

### Server Components (Default)
```typescript
// app/page.tsx
// Server Component by default - no 'use client'
export default async function Page() {
  // Can directly fetch data
  const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data');
  const json = await data.json();

  return <div>{json.title}</div>;
}
```

**Benefits:**
- Zero JavaScript sent to client
- Direct database/API access
- Automatic code splitting
- Better SEO

### Client Components
```typescript
// components/Counter.tsx
'use client';

import { useState } from 'react';

export function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  return <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>{count}</button>;
}
```

**Use when you need:**
- State (useState, useReducer)
- Effects (useEffect)
- Event handlers
- Browser APIs
- Custom hooks

## Data Fetching Patterns

### Parallel Data Fetching
```typescript
// app/page.tsx
export default async function Page() {
  // Fetch in parallel
  const [users, products, reviews] = await Promise.all([
    fetch('https://api.example.com/users').then(r => r.json()),
    fetch('https://api.example.com/products').then(r => r.json()),
    fetch('https://api.example.com/reviews').then(r => r.json()),
  ]);

  return <div>{/* render */}</div>;
}
```

### Sequential Data Fetching (When Needed)
```typescript
export default async function Page() {
  // First fetch
  const user = await fetch('https://api.example.com/user').then(r => r.json());

  // Then fetch data that depends on user
  const profile = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/profile/${user.id}`)
    .then(r => r.json());

  return <div>{/* render */}</div>;
}
```

### Streaming with Suspense
